This Act applies to any of the following persons who does one or both of the following:

(a) sells, or offers or exposes for sale or hire, as a trader, or for use in connection with trade, or offers or exposes for use in connection with trade, alcohol or any of the following products or compounds in any quantity:

(i) the following spirits (other than gin): beer, porter or stout or spirituous liquor;

(ii) the following distilled spirits (other than spirits authorised by or approved in writing by the Governor‑General) that are in bulk and are to be used for purposes other than the production of spirits; and

(iii) any product containing these spirits;

(b) distributes any alcohol or product referred to in paragraph (a) that bears a marking or logo in accordance with section 2.1;

and, for the purposes of this Act, alcohol or a product referred to in that paragraph is to be taken to be a product manufactured in Australia for Australian use.
